// Single source of truth for the site-wide "which country am I browsing/
// listing in" concept (Listing.country) — mirrors soukmar/src/app/models/
// country.model.ts and soukmar-backend/src/lib/countries.ts EXACTLY (same
// COUNTRIES array, same CITIES_BY_COUNTRY curated set), via the same
// generation script already used for soukmar-android's CountryModels.kt —
// no hand-transcription across ~193 countries. If the web list changes,
// re-run the extraction rather than editing this file by hand.
//
// Codes are ISO 3166-1 alpha-2, same as web/Android, so this stays
// interchangeable with the backend's Listing.country column. Country
// *names* are never hand-translated here — Locale(identifier:).localizedString(forRegionCode:)
// is the Swift equivalent of Intl.DisplayNames (CLDR-backed), used at call
// sites instead of a hardcoded name table.

